                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f44c87f-863a-357f-9a27-4b8eec9f33db",
                        "entry_id": "60ae30db-1e86-39f2-b360-c08363ff0785",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A reluctance to take advantage of pragmatic opportunities that present themselves, usually because of ideological or theological purity."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "104ebf5b-a146-40ae-b40a-23f7bdee02fd",
                                "sense_id": "2f44c87f-863a-357f-9a27-4b8eec9f33db",
                                "text": "And I do not believe in the inopportunism of Socialists."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "150d3e9b-15cf-42d6-b48c-b037458f008d",
                                "sense_id": "2f44c87f-863a-357f-9a27-4b8eec9f33db",
                                "text": "Who would risk a schism in a mere question of inopportunism?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7478416a-42ce-4b3b-9afc-97112e5acd6d",
                                "sense_id": "2f44c87f-863a-357f-9a27-4b8eec9f33db",
                                "text": "When we still had a situation where we had to reckon with revolutionary spasms, we faced what was called the 'inopportunism' of the Left, a tendency that had to be overcome."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
